WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.860
Matsukaze has finally gotten around Seidouzan's trap!

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:09.820
Tsurugi!

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.780
Death Drop!

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.330
Shoot Br-

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.150
Goal!

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.040
Raimon catches up!

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.020
All right.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:27.500
Yes!

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.500
You did it! Great!

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.970
Now it's gotten interesting.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.640
Great, the plan worked!

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.300
You did it, Tenma!

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.250
Awesome, now they're picking up a tailwind.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:46.620
They aren't pulling back a step even against Seidouzan!

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.020
I wanted to see Shin-sama shoot...

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.480
That's true.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.370
Tsurugi's shoot brings the score to a 1-1 tie!

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.910
Will this carry on the momentum?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.570
They just might make it!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.120
We're tied now.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.660
We caught up!

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.690
I'm starting to feel like we'll actually win this!

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:48.530
Yeah!

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.150
We'll settle this match once and for all!

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:53.910
Tenma!

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.180
We're putting pressure on them.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.130
Let's keep up the momentum!

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.070
Okay!

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.910
What'll you do, Gouenji?

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.450
The match resumes with Seidouzan's kickoff!

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:16.340
Hyuuga!

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:17.830
He got past me!

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.340
Hyuuga heads up to Raimon with his skillful dribbling!

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:22.860
Go, Hyuuga!

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.090
Leave it to me!

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:25.870
I'll stop him!

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.390
Matsukaze steps onto Hyuuga's path!

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.350
Round Spark!

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:40.070
Hyuuga breaks past Matsukaze with a hissatsu technique!

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.900
Koizaki!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.070
Kurosaki!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.880
Kurosaki takes the ball!

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.950
He dodges Kurumada's slide tackle and heads for the goal!

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.100
Kariya!

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.640
You won't get past me!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:56.710
An Avatar?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.650
Flame Demon Gazard!

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.890
Bakunetsu Storm!

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.990
Hunter's Net!

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.430
Fence Of Gaia!

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.920
Goal!

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:38.470
Seidouzan's captain Kurosaki shows his volition by scoring with an Avatar shoot!

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:40.380
All right!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.740
Splendid, Kurosaki!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.960
They got us.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.340
An Avatar shoot?

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:52.590
Seidouzan isn't trained in just technique and power, but also in mentality.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.350
I suppose that's what you'd expect from Gouenji.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.970
Gouenji, I can feel it...

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:03.760
Your feelings for soccer through Seidouzan's plays.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.320
This is Seidouzan's soccer.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:25.670
Seidouzan is indeed a step above Raimon, Senguuji-sama.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.860
This is not heading in a good direction.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.840
What's wrong, sir?

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:35.200
Seidouzan's soccer is meant to demonstrate the regulation of teamwork.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.770
But the players are starting to take action outside of that regulation.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.180
This isn't the soccer that Fifth Sector desires.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:43.760
But...

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.130
Nevertheless, I'll let them do what they want for now.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.620
The time to use Dragon Link has come.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.810
You found out what Dragon Link is?

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.440
Yeah.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:02.180
I just barely managed to find it.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:04.300
So what is it?

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:06.710
I can't believe it.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.160
Dragon Link is...

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.760
Raimon's counterattack has begun!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.350
The new captain Matsukaze comes up with his dribbling!

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:20.830
Good, the morale hasn't dropped even though we lost a point.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.490
You won't get past me!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.040
All right, I'll use Soyokaze Step.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.250
Air Bullet!

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:38.720
Tenma!

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.080
They got him!

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:41.720
Seidouzan...

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.780
Every one of them is an amazing player.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.270
I can't find any blind spots in their offense or defense.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.380
Kurosaki!

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.640
Leave it to me!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.800
Tsutsumi!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.700
The Mist!

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.610
Kirino-senpai!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.030
Nishiki!

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:09.650
Nice one!

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.180
Raimon has the ball again!

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:14.690
Kurama!

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:16.370
Tsurugi!

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.510
Tsurugi takes the ball!

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.160
Will he shoot?

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:21.710
Not while we're here!

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:30.610
Sengoku War God Musashi!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.870
Bushin Renzan!

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.870
Shoot Break!

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.400
Goal!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.870
It's in!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.770
Raimon makes an Avatar shoot this time to take back a point!

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.590
A truly seesaw game! You just can't take your eyes off this amazing match!

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.210
All right!

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:12.590
It's tied!

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.540
This is a good game.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:18.430
Both teams are using everything in their power to fight.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.350
That's the end of the first half!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.940
The score is 2-2!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.940
Raimon and Seidouzan meet half-time with a tie!

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.460
You guys are pretty good too.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:37.370
But Seidouzan has no word like "loss" in its dictionary.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:41.670
We at Raimon have been fighting with everything we've got up to this point.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.750
We won't ever lose.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.100
Fight with everything in the second half as well.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.580
We'll respond with our everything too.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.060
Seidouzan is fighting with its pride on the line.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:59.580
We have to make sure not to bring shame to Raimon's name either.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.560
Ishido Shuuji...

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.500
So is that your answer to me?

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.820
Inazuma Eleven...

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:29.770
GO!

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:35.050
Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.890
Isn't this awesome, Tenma?!

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:48.810
You're fighting evenly against Seidouzan. That's impressive!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:50.190
Yeah...

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.040
What's wrong, Tenma?

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.960
I wonder if I'm doing Captain Shindou's job properly...

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.770
You are!

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:02.800
You took back the goals they took, and as far as I see, you have the upper hand!

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.120
Have confidence.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.020
Yeah, yeah!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.310
Yeah...

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.460
You're doing a great job as captain.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.040
Thank you.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:19.880
I feel like I'm managing this through because I'm pulling Captain Shindou and everyone else's feelings with me.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:21.550
But I...

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.710
Don't worry.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:26.200
We're all here behind you.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.900
We'll be sure to support you!

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:33.040
Yes, I'll do my best to fill Captain Shindou's role.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.570
We'll cheer you on!

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.370
Thanks.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.620
Is it really a lot of pressure being captain?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.090
Yeah.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.110
But I'm happy that we got to have a match against Seidouzan.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:52.360
They're fearsome, but they're all playing soccer for real.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.340
I think they're really a good team.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:58.470
I see! I want to play on the field too.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.830
Tenma, do your part for me too!

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:01.610
Yeah.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.260
Hey now, what's the point of complimenting the opponent?

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.830
Oh, right.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:08.260
But I know what Tenma's talking about.

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:10.370
Those guys have pretty good guts.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:16.290
It's hard to believe that the Holy Emperor is the coach of that team.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.260
The team he raised...

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:22.820
If it's this amazing of a team, maybe...

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.290
Tenma.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:25.700
Yes, sir?

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:29.930
The strength of a captain is most needed during a crisis.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:36.260
It's up to you to be able to support everyone on the team when that time comes.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.840
Don't forget that.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.800
Support everyone during a crisis?

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.290
Yes, sir. I'll do my best!

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:48.770
Holy Emperor, your orders.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.020
I'll leave it to you guys.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:06.590
Take pride in your results up to this point and fight freely.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:09.290
I have faith in your soccer.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:11.950
Freely...

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.420
You want us to fight freely without any orders?

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.950
You can overcome any obstacle no matter how difficult they may be.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:23.470
At least, that is how I intended to raise Seidouzan.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:24.900
Yes, sir!

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.010
I understand.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.890
We'll use everything in our power to defeat Raimon!

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:31.670
Got it?

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:35.830
Hit them with all the skills you've fostered up until now to obtain victory!

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:37.560
Go on without hesitation!

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.040
Yes, sir!

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.260
We've finally made it to the last stage.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.280
With this, the revolution will-

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:49.790
Holy Emperor.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.670
Senguuji-sama has summoned you.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.670
I loved soccer so much I didn't know what to do with myself.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.380
I just had to play soccer no matter what.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.620
That's all I had going for me.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:15.460
There he is!

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.060
Don't let him get away!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.330
Geez, what a troublemaker!

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:23.220
Hey! Give back the ball you stole!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:32.700
But the sudden impulse that occurred from having those feelings stole soccer away from me.

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.960
We've brought the Holy Emperor.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.440
The second half is about to begin.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:47.590
What business do you have?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.350
You've disappointed me, Ishido-san.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:57.480
You allowed the symbol of Fifth Sector, Seidouzan, to struggle at a tie.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.650
This is the reality.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:03.180
The rebellion that Raimon started...

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:06.190
I've heard that <i>you're</i>  the one pulling the strings behind that.

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:10.920
Are you ordering Seidouzan to go easy on them?

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.550
Seidouzan is playing with everything they have.

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:18.160
They are Fifth Sector's greatest team, with everything the syndicate stands for instilled into them.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:24.170
It is just that Raimon is another excellent team like Seidouzan.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:28.840
Are you saying that Seidouzan and Raimon are equal when they're at their best?

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:34.010
This is a fight between everything that makes managed soccer and everything that makes free soccer.

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:37.730
If it weren't so, the true answer wouldn't reveal itself.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:42.730
If Seidouzan wins against Raimon in this match,

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:48.860
I will place my full intent into serving Fifth Sector.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.200
As your servant.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:54.310
The answer will reveal itself soon.

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:56.230
Answer?

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.890
That's already been decided.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:02.460
Ishido Shuuji, you're dismissed from your position as Seidouzan's coach.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:06.020
I'll take command of the team from here.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:07.880
I understand.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:11.430
That is, with the players that I've raised.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:16.100
Seidouzan will be reborn as a new team!

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:45.040
You can't get a hold of Endou-kun's cell?

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.840
He's probably on the pitch already.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.420
We have to tell him as soon as possible.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:53.580
Dragon Link's true identity... and the dangers it holds!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.680
Hey!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.390
Look at Amanomikado Stadium!

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.080
What's this?!

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:05.920
Amanomikado Stadium is changing shape before our very eyes!

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.220
Seidouzan versus Raimon!

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:17.850
The second half of the Holy Road finals is about to start in the Amanomikado Stadium turned sky-high!

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.300
E-Excuse me!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.170
We have a change in players.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:43.580
Seidouzan will be changing its coach and <i>all</i>  of its players!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:53.310
This member change is under the Fifth Law that allows Fifth Sector to change the rules!

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.180
You can't just <i>do</i>  that!

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.480
They changed the coaches and all the players?

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:00.830
They <i>really</i>  don't want us to win.

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:07.540
What happened to Kurosaki-san and the others?

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.630
Don't know.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.250
We're Dragon Link.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:15.430
We're the ultimate eleven with the highest supremacy in Fifth Sector.

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.440
Dragon Link...

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:22.590
You'll experience a new dimension of soccer compared to the first half.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.790
Better be prepared.

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:29.810
Replacing Coach Ishido Shuuji is Senguuji Daigo.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:34.540
And all of the players are ones who have never played in official matches before!

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.570
They really did it.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:41.140
Here is Seidouzan's new lineup.

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:45.100
The captain is the goalkeeper, Senguuji Yamato!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:55.400
Every player was changed out...

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:58.660
What happened to Kurosaki-san and the others?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.050
Focus, Tenma.

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:01.510
Yes!

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.950
They're pretty startled.

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.440
Let's get to the real deal.

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:12.550
Fifth Sector's true soccer is about to start.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:16.570
Matsukaze Tenma, I'll have you learn...

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:20.570
...that there is power in this world you cannot defy.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.070
Gouenji...

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.290
It seems the Holy Emperor...

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:29.570
No, it seems Gouenji was removed from his position by Senguuji.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.490
Why did he have to leave his position as coach?

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:36.960
He hadn't been trying to control soccer. 
 He'd been trying to protect it.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:43.960
Gouenji became the Holy Emperor to keep an eye on Fifth Sector and Senguuji's movements.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.500
Gouenji-san?

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:50.990
He himself was conflicted between which was right, managed soccer or free soccer.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:52.400
But...

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.560
It's all right.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:58.150
The revolutionary wind we've stirred up won't ever settle back down.

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:09.040
We at Dragon Link have come to teach you what Fifth Sector's soccer is like.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.120
What do you mean?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.610
I created Fifth Sector.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:17.020
Dad.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:18.990
You're...!

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.760
<i>Do you like soccer?</i>

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:24.670
<i>If you do, then just imagine...</i>

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:27.390
<i>The pain of never being able to play soccer anymore.</i>

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:33.650
Only those who are blessed with a good environment are able to learn to play soccer and aim to become pros.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:38.230
As a youth, I wasn't even given the right to play.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:43.240
Just one soccer ball caused my dad to lose soccer altogether.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:50.740
Regretting my crime, I established Fifth Sector, where anyone would have an equal chance to play soccer.

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:53.700
Soccer needs to be managed.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:58.430
That's wrong.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:02.630
Real soccer isn't something that someone manages!

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.200
There's the start of the second half!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.430
Will Raimon keep up the momentum from the first half?

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:14.890
Gotou passes it to the front line where none of his teammates are!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.870
Was that a miskick?

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:22.020
Seidouzan disregards the tied score and tightens up their defense!

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:24.270
These guys...

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:25.940
What're they thinking?

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.370
We'll just have to go at them!

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:31.410
Kirino-senpai, pass to Hamano-senpai!

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:33.960
I've got it!

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.090
Something's creepy about them.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:39.660
Hamano!

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:40.470
Yeah!

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:44.340
All right, I'll make the winning point!

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.350
You won't get past us.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:55.940
Elite Soldier Pawn!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.100
I knew it.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:04.760
What's this?!

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:08.230
Seidouzan suddenly brings out four Avatars!

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:11.230
This is a truly amazing spectacle!

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:19.450
All four forwards brought out Avatars?

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:57.000
I can't believe Seidouzan changed every one of their players!

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:59.890
How should I fight them as the team captain?

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:03.980
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 Heroic! The Final Holy Battle!!

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:05.730
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:17.910
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:26.740
The strength of a captain is most needed during a crisis.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:27.630
That's all!
